ang/issues/38#issuecomment-5696692508"},"message":"Human retest found the replacement packaged UI left all provider controls disabled because module startup awaited Tauri event-listener registration. Fixed on spike/tauri-rig-tutor in 262c7e0: controls initialize independently, Connect / Save remains immediately available, provider actions explain when the event channel is still starting, and listener timeout/failure is shown in the status region. Rebuilt the macOS package; live OpenCode and ChatGPT validation remains pending.","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1789558338,"nonce":"z0zrAH3C6bj/uxIwJGHUZng5Z0c=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOUKdEis8AAAABU41xRA","github-url":"https://github.com/ff6347/giclang/issues/38#issuecomment-5696745796"},"message":"The next human retest exposed the actual event-channel failure: Connect / Save worked, but the packaged app reported that the tutor connection was still starting. Root cause was missing Tauri v2 ACL permission for frontend listen(). Fixed in 89db6a9 by adding an explicit tutor-events capability scoped to the main window with only core:event:allow-listen, referencing it from tauri.conf.json, and adding a verifier regression check. Cargo tests/check, UI build, capability-aware Tauri packaging, and targeted formatting passed. Live provider retest remains pending.","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1789559188,"nonce":"mc5pVr0i2DVQp96eLSE9oqsKyVY=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOUKdEis8AAAABU4_qzA","github-url":"https://github.com/ff6347/giclang/issues/38#issuecomment-5696907980"},"message":"Human validation now passes OpenCode Zen streaming and the ChatGPT device-auth flow. The first authenticated ChatGPT completion failed with only the generic safe error. Commit 9a5fbf4 adds a selectable in-app diagnostic log and preserves the credential boundary: it records lifecycle stages, model/endpoint, account-ID presence as a boolean, HTTP status, and whitelisted provider error fields; it excludes keys, tokens, account IDs, 